Room: the engine framework is RoomCore.framework (binary RoomCore), not
"$chrome_product_full_name Framework": chrome_framework_name, kFrameworkName
and the helpers' dlopen path. The Swift app imports it as a Clang module,
which needs a framework named after the module (//room/build/config.gni).

content/public/app/BUILD.gn (added 2026-10-04, Phase 3.1b-2): in
non-component builds libaperitif's install name is built from
"$chrome_product_full_name Framework.framework", while chrome/BUILD.gn's
installnametool -change for the Aperitif helpers looks for
$chrome_framework_name.framework, so the change never matched. Reproducible
release-build failure (args/release.gn, out/release, 57,373 of 57,727 steps):
//chrome:verify_libraries_chrome_helper_app_aperitif_alerts failed with
"Room Helper (Aperitif Alerts)" linking
@executable_path/../Frameworks/Room Framework.framework/Versions/154.0.8037.58/Libraries/libaperitif.dylib
where @executable_path/../../../../Libraries/libaperitif.dylib is expected.
The component build is unaffected (@rpath install name).

